{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Shared kitchen/bath exemption narrowed","requirement":"A rental unit where the tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord is exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","key_value":"exemption condition: landlord resided on same property at tenancy start","coverage_conditions":"Tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities with landlord.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","unit_type":"rental unit sharing kitchen/bath with landlord","property_type":"same property as landlord","tenure":"any"},"exemptions":"Exempt only if landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | CHANGES TO EXEMPTIONS AND RENT ORDINANCE COVERAGE FOR SOME UNITS","quoted_span":"Where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord, the unit will be exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Government-owned or subsidized units covered","requirement":"Government-owned or -subsidized rental units, such as Section 8 and Shelter Plus Care, are now either fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance; coverage depends on unit type and whether federal, state, or administrative law exempts the unit from rent control.","key_value":"coverage: fully or partially covered","coverage_conditions":"Government-owned or -subsidized rental units, including Section 8, Shelter Plus Care, VASH, LIHTC, California Community Housing Agency, HOME, City of Berkeley Housing Trust Fund, Mental Health Safety Act, and specified HUD-related subsidies.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","property_type":"government-owned or subsidized rental unit","subsidy":["Section 8","Shelter Plus Care","VASH Voucher","LIHTC","California Community Housing Agency","HOME","City of Berkeley Housing Trust Fund","Mental Health Safety Act","Rent Supplement Program","Section 8 Loan Management Set Aside","Project-based Section 8"],"coverage":"fully or partially covered"},"exemptions":"Units may be partially covered if federal law, state law, or administrative regulation prohibits rent control.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | CHANGES TO EXEMPTIONS AND RENT ORDINANCE COVERAGE FOR SOME UNITS","quoted_span":"Government-owned or -subsidized rental units like Section 8 and Shelter + Care units are Now Fully or Partially Covered by the Rent Ordinance","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Government-subsidized units must register and pay annual fee","requirement":"Landlords of government-owned or -subsidized units must register them with the Rent Board as either fully or partially covered and pay an annual registration fee.","key_value":"registration: required; annual fee: required","coverage_conditions":"Government-owned or -subsidized units.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","property_type":"government-owned or subsidized rental unit","landlord_obligation":"register and pay fee"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | CHANGES TO EXEMPTIONS AND RENT ORDINANCE COVERAGE FOR SOME UNITS","quoted_span":"Landlords of government-owned or -subsidized units must register them with the Rent Board as either fully or partially covered, and pay an annual registration fee.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Nonpayment eviction requires rental debt at least one month FMR","requirement":"For a landlord to evict for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) for a unit of equivalent size in the Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR area for the fiscal year in which rent is demanded.","key_value":"threshold: >= 1 month FMR","coverage_conditions":"Covered rental units subject to just cause; nonpayment of rent.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","unit_type":"covered rental unit","ground":"nonpayment of rent"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | CHANGES TO GROUNDS FOR EVICTION AND EVICTION NOTICE REQUIREMENTS","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"No eviction for refusing to sign substantially similar lease","requirement":"A landlord cannot evict a tenant for failing to sign a substantially similar lease upon expiration of a fixed-term lease.","key_value":"prohibited eviction ground: failure to sign substantially similar lease","coverage_conditions":"Covered rental units subject to just cause; fixed-term lease expiration.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","unit_type":"covered rental unit","ground":"failure to sign substantially similar lease"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | CHANGES TO GROUNDS FOR EVICTION AND EVICTION NOTICE REQUIREMENTS","quoted_span":"A landlord cannot evict a tenant for failing to sign a substantially similar lease upon expiration of a fixed-term lease.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Material lease breach eviction restrictions","requirement":"In any notice terminating tenancy for a lease breach, the landlord must clearly describe the alleged breach, demonstrate that the tenant’s behavior was unreasonable, and may not evict for lease breaches that do not cause actual harm. Material lease terms only include mutually agreed terms, and the alleged violation must cause substantial actual damage.","key_value":"ground: material lease breach; required: actual harm + unreasonable behavior + detailed notice","coverage_conditions":"Covered rental units subject to just cause; alleged violation of material lease term.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","unit_type":"covered rental unit","ground":"material lease breach"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | CHANGES TO GROUNDS FOR EVICTION AND EVICTION NOTICE REQUIREMENTS","quoted_span":"In any notice terminating a tenancy for a lease breach, the landlord must clearly describe the alleged breach. The landlord must demonstrate that the tenant’s behavior was unreasonable, and may not evict tenants for lease breaches that do not cause the landlord any actual harm.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction notices must include Rent Board information","requirement":"Any notice terminating a tenancy must contain a statement that advice about the notice is available from the Rent Board, the current phone number for the Rent Board’s Housing counseling services, and the current address of the Rent Board’s website.","key_value":"required notice content: Rent Board advice, phone, website","coverage_conditions":"Any notice terminating a tenancy in a covered unit.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","document_type":"notice terminating tenancy"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | CHANGES TO GROUNDS FOR EVICTION AND EVICTION NOTICE REQUIREMENTS","quoted_span":"Any notice terminating a tenancy must contain a statement that advice about the notice is available from the Rent Board, the current phone number for the Rent Board’s Housing counseling services, and the current address of the Rent Board’s website.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction notices and lawsuits must be filed within 3 business days","requirement":"The landlord must file with the Rent Board a copy of any notice to terminate a tenancy, notice to quit, and summons and complaint no later than three business days after the tenant was served with the document.","key_value":"filing deadline: 3 business days","coverage_conditions":"Eviction-related documents served on tenant in covered unit.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","document_type":["notice to terminate tenancy","notice to quit","summons and complaint"]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | CHANGES TO GROUNDS FOR EVICTION AND EVICTION NOTICE REQUIREMENTS","quoted_span":"The landlord must file with the Rent Board a copy of any notice to terminate a tenancy, notice to quit, and summons and complaint no later than three business days after the tenant was served with the document.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Utility charges must be in base rent unless separately metered","requirement":"A landlord may charge a tenant in a fully covered unit for utilities only if the cost of utilities is part of the base rent, or the utility service is separately metered and the lease requires the tenant to place the utility in the tenant’s name.","key_value":"utility charge allowed: part of base rent OR separately metered/tenant account","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered rental units; tenancies starting on or after February 6, 2024.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","unit_type":"fully covered rental unit","tenancy_start":">= 2024-02-06","charge_type":"utilities"},"exemptions":"Separately metered utility with account in tenant’s name as specified in lease.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-02-06","citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | NEW RULES ABOUT PAYING FOR UTILITIES","quoted_span":"Utility charges must be a set amount incorporated into the base rent at the start of a tenancy unless the utility is separately metered and the account is in the tenant’s name as specified in the lease.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Utility cost may be added to rent ceiling by petition","requirement":"A landlord charging a tenant for utilities separately from rent on or after February 6, 2024, may file a petition with the Rent Board to add the average cost of utilities to the rent ceiling; increases must be made through the petition process, though the hearing may be waived if parties agree and standards are met.","key_value":"petition: allowed to add average utility cost to rent ceiling","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered units; landlord charging utilities separately on or after February 6, 2024.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","unit_type":"fully covered rental unit","charge_type":"utilities","effective_date":">= 2024-02-06"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-02-06","citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | NEW RULES ABOUT PAYING FOR UTILITIES","quoted_span":"A landlord who is charging a tenant for utilities separately from rent on or after February 6, 2024, may file a petition with the Rent Board to add the average cost of utilities to the rent ceiling.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant right to organize and petition for rent decrease","requirement":"Tenants on certain properties have an enforceable right to create tenant associations and engage in organizing activities; landlords and tenant associations must confer in good faith, and tenants may petition for a decrease in rent if this right is violated.","key_value":"right: organize; remedy: petition for rent decrease; duty: confer in good faith","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who live on certain properties.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","tenant_right":"organize","remedy":"rent decrease petition"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | NEW TENANT RIGHT TO ORGANIZE","quoted_span":"Tenants have an enforceable right to organize and may petition for a decrease in rent if this right is violated.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Capital improvement rent increases limited to completed improvements","requirement":"Landlords can only file a petition for rent increases for completed capital improvements and can no longer petition to preliminarily authorize rent increases for planned capital improvements.","key_value":"eligible capital improvements: completed only","coverage_conditions":"Owners petitioning for rent increases for capital improvements.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","petition_type":"capital improvement rent increase"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | LANDLORDS CAN NO LONGER FILE A PETITION FOR RENT INCREASES FOR PLANNED CAPITAL IMPROVEMENTS","quoted_span":"Owners may only petition for rent increases for completed capital improvements, rather than planned capital improvements.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Partially covered units must report new tenancies within 15 days","requirement":"Owners of partially covered units must report new tenancies to the Rent Board within 15 days of the tenancy’s start date and update tenancy information annually during the registration billing cycle.","key_value":"reporting deadline: 15 days; annual update: required","coverage_conditions":"Partially covered rental units.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","unit_type":"partially covered rental unit","landlord_obligation":"tenancy reporting"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | CHANGE TO TENANCY REPORTING REQUIREMENTS FOR LANDLORDS OF PARTIALLY COVERED UNITS","quoted_span":"Owners of partially covered units must now report new tenancies to the Rent Board within 15 days of the tenancy’s start date.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Annual General Adjustment capped at 5%","requirement":"The maximum Annual General Adjustment (AGA) is 5%; if the Rent Ordinance formula results in an AGA greater than 5%, the Board may not approve more than 5%. The cap does not prevent a landlord from using banked unused AGAs from previous years to raise rent to the rent ceiling.","key_value":"AGA cap: 5%","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered rental units; AGA set by Rent Board.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","unit_type":"fully covered rental unit","rent_increase_type":"Annual General Adjustment"},"exemptions":"Banked (unused) AGAs from previous years may still be implemented to raise rent to the rent ceiling.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | CHANGES ANNUAL GENERAL ADJUSTMENT (AGA) CAP TO 5%","quoted_span":"Annual General Adjustments are capped at a maximum of 5%.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Annual adjustment of owner move-in eviction relocation assistance","requirement":"The Rent Board must make inflationary adjustments to owner move-in eviction relocation assistance amounts each year.","key_value":"relocation assistance: annual inflationary adjustment required","coverage_conditions":"Owner move-in evictions.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","eviction_type":"owner move-in","obligation":"relocation assistance adjustment"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | THE RENT BOARD IS NOW REQUIRED TO ANNUALLY ADJUST OWNER MOVE-IN EVICTION RELOCATION ASSISTANCE PAYMENTS","quoted_span":"Yearly adjustments to owner move-in eviction relocation assistance payments are now mandatory.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Rent Board empowered to fine for late tenancy reporting","requirement":"Measure BB gives the Rent Board power to impose fines for failing to report new tenancies within fifteen days of the tenancy start date. The Board must adopt regulations to impose any fines; the measure does not itself create a fine system.","key_value":"penalty: fines for failure to report new tenancies within 15 days","coverage_conditions":"Failure to report new tenancies within 15 days.","applicability":{"jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","landlord_obligation":"timely tenancy reporting","enforcement":"Rent Board fines"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Rent Board may impose fines for failure to report new tenancies within 15 days; Board must adopt regulations.","effective_date":null,"citation":"https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/laws-regulations/measure-bb-changes-berkeleys-rent-ordinance | RENT BOARD EMPOWERED TO IMPLEMENT FINES FOR THE FAILURE TO TIMELY REPORT NEW TENANCIES","quoted_span":"Measure BB gives the Rent Board the power to impose fines for failing to report new tenancies within fifteen days of the tenancy start date.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
